From da88b5a56c81268eb688df86223151f52dceee7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sfermigier@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:48:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] cmake: match base.pri mac defines (LINUX, _LINUX, MAC)

core_mac in Common/base.pri is `DEFINES += LINUX _LINUX MAC _MAC`.
Upstream spells "POSIX-ish" _LINUX/LINUX and real Linux __linux__, so a mac
build wants all four; defining only _MAC leaves platform branches with no
arm to take.

Directory.cpp is where this bites: NSDirectory::GetFiles has a __linux__
branch and a `#if defined(MAC) || defined(_IOS)` branch, and we matched
neither. allfontsgen exited 0 having found no fonts at all.
---
 common.cmake | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common.cmake b/common.cmake
index 5372e1fd5a..764237d40c 100644
--- a/common.cmake
+++ b/common.cmake
@@ -264,7 +264,15 @@ if( LINUX )
         UNICODE
     )
 elseif( APPLE )
+    # base.pri's core_mac is `DEFINES += LINUX _LINUX MAC _MAC`: upstream uses
+    # _LINUX/LINUX to mean "POSIX-ish" and __linux__ for actual Linux, so a mac
+    # build gets all four. Directory.cpp is the reason this is not optional --
+    # its mac branch tests bare MAC, and with neither MAC nor __linux__ set,
+    # NSDirectory::GetFiles has no implementation and silently returns nothing.
     set(COMMON_DEFINES
+        LINUX
+        _LINUX
+        MAC
         _MAC
         _REENTRANT
         CRYPTOPP_DISABLE_ASM
